Generic single-database configuration.

Known Schema Drift Reconciliation (20261019_120000)
-------------------------------------------------
This online-only migration restores the confirmed missing schema objects from
20260930_120000, 20261002_120000 and 20261006_120000:
- fabs.is_migrated and fabs.migration_source, plus the migration flag index.
- accounts.is_active and its index.
- performance_static_data and subcontractor_weekly_labor, their indexes and
	updated_by foreign keys.

Existing values are preserved. Newly created flags use the original defaults
(is_migrated=false, is_active=true). Missing performance tables are created
empty; historical financial data cannot be recovered by this migration.
Incompatible definitions, duplicate unique keys, orphaned foreign keys or missing
required values cause failure rather than guessing, deleting or coercing data.
Take a database backup before applying. PostgreSQL runs the repair transactionally
with a 5-second lock timeout and a 60-second statement timeout. Downgrade is
intentionally refused because restored objects may already contain important data.

Staging currently records the server-only merge revision 043a0c77f7ac, whose
parents include 20261017_120000. The reconciliation also follows 20261017_120000;
it deliberately does not reference server-only migration files absent from this
repository. Preserve all those server files when deploying the new migration.

From /var/www/staging/backend/alphagranite-backend, after verifying DATABASE_URL
targets alpha_granite_staging:

		docker compose --env-file .env.staging -p ag_staging exec web alembic heads
		docker compose --env-file .env.staging -p ag_staging exec web alembic upgrade heads
		docker compose --env-file .env.staging -p ag_staging exec web alembic current

On this staging graph, current should then list both 043a0c77f7ac and
20261019_120000. This is intentional: do not stamp over either revision or
downgrade. A single canonical head requires bringing the server-only branches
into version control and committing a merge migration after both histories are
available. A migration on the local chain alone can use upgrade head.

This is a targeted repair, not a complete certification of all database objects
against application metadata or the server-only branches. Subsequent schema
changes must continue to use normal reviewed migrations.

Focused tests (SQLite by default; PostgreSQL integration requires an isolated
database named schema_reconciliation_test):

		python -m pytest tests/test_schema_reconciliation.py -q

Set SCHEMA_RECONCILIATION_TEST_URL to a SQLAlchemy psycopg2 URL for that dedicated
test database to exercise PostgreSQL behavior. Tests roll back their changes.